  "title": "epan: fix memory leaks in column format and SRT table filter parsing",
  "description": "Summary:\n\nThis MR resolves two heap memory leaks (CWE-401) on error return paths in libwireshark (epan):\n\n1\\. epan/column.c (parse_column_format):\n\n   col_custom_fields was dynamically allocated via g_strdup() when cust_format_info-\\>len \\> 0. If parsing the subsequent occurrence token failed (e.g. invalid numeric string), the function freed fmt_copy and unreferenced cust_format_info, but returned false without freeing col_custom_fields.\n\n2\\. epan/srt_table.c (srt_table_get_filter):\n\n   cmd_str was dynamically allocated using srt_table_get_tap_string(). When an SRT tap's parameter callback (srt-\\>param_cb) reported an error (\\*err != NULL) due to malformed tap arguments, the function executed an early return without freeing cmd_str.\n\nChanges:\n\n\\- Added g_free(col_custom_fields) before returning false on occurrence parsing error in parse_column_format().\n\n\\- Added g_free(cmd_str) before returning when srt-\\>param_cb returns an error in srt_table_get_filter().\n\n\\- Validated with unit test harnesses confirming zero leaked allocations on error paths.",
